1
00:00:03,159 --> 00:00:04,370
Lesson 17.

2
00:00:04,879 --> 00:00:07,110
Carol tells Bob the good news.

3
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:11,150
Carol phones Bob to tell him the cookies are selling very well,

4
00:00:11,179 --> 00:00:13,589
and that she needs another 1000 by the morning.

5
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:16,929
Bob isn't sure he can make the cookies so quickly,

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,709
but Carol insists.

7
00:00:20,619 --> 00:00:24,589
Bob, your wife's cookies are selling like hotcakes.

8
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,809
How many did you sell, Carol?

9
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:28,889
We've sold out.

10
00:00:28,739 --> 00:00:31,489
I need more right away.

11
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:36,030
Bring me another 1000 by tomorrow at 9 a.m.

12
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,449
That's a tall order, Carol.

13
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:40,570
Don't blow it, Bob.

14
00:00:41,259 --> 00:00:44,549
Susan scrumptious cookies could really take off.

15
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,409
I know, but I'm not sure we have enough time to bake all those cookies.

16
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,589
Bake all night if you have to.

17
00:00:53,119 --> 00:00:54,369
Burn the midnight oil.

18
00:00:54,219 --> 00:00:59,390
If you work hard now, you'll be sitting pretty in a few years.

19
00:00:59,619 --> 00:01:03,530
Rest assured that I'll do my best to deliver the goods.

20
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:07,070
Okay, now let's stop the chitchat.

21
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:08,590
You've got work to do.

